BSP-Yocto-NXP-i.MX95-ALPHA2                                           2025-03-06
================================================================================
- Linux kernel v6.12.34-2.1.0-phy9 (LTS kernel)
- U-Boot v2025.04-2.1.0-phy8
- System Manager 6.12.34-2.1.0-phy1
- Optional Executable Image 6.12.34-2.1.0-phy1
- Yocto 5.2.4 (walnascar)

NOTE:
This is an ALPHA release and has not been tested for full functionality. It is
possible that some features are not working correctly.

Tested Yocto Images:
--------------------
- phytec-chromium-image
- phytec-headless-image
- phytec-qt6demo-image
- phytec-vision-image

Build Environment:
------------------
- Ubuntu 24.04 64-bit

Supported Machines:
-------------------
imx95-phyflex-libra-rdk-2

Changes:
--------
- New naming scheme for product (dts, yocto machine, Kconfig names)
- Update machine revision (new hardware)
- boot flow (ampliphy-boot; changes to U-Boot environment variables)
- changed from Ax SoC revision support to B0 SoC revision support
- USB Host is now supported in U-Boot

Defeatured:
-----------
- imx95-libra-fpsc-1
- support for Ax SoC revision

New Features:
-------------
- Camera support
  * VM-024 phyCAM-M
- Chromium support (chromium image)
- Introduction of ampliphy-boot
- RS232/485 support
- PWM fan support
- TPM support
- USB-C device and host mode support
- VPU support

Other Features:
---------------
- Boot from e.MMC
- Boot from SD card
- Boot via USB serial download (uuu)
- LVDS display support
- GPU support
- RTC support
- USB 2.0 support (Linux)
- Debug UART support
- GBit Ethernet support (SoM + Carrier board)
- Power Management support (suspend + frequency scaling)
- U-Boot standard boot (https://docs.u-boot.org/en/v2025.04/develop/bootstd.html#u-boot-standard-boot)
- NPU support
- Camera support
    * VM-016 phyCAM-M / phyCAM-L
    * VM-017 phyCAM-M / phyCAM-L
    * VM-020 phyCAM-M / phyCAM-L
- ISP support (Debayer, AEC, AWB)

Known Issues and Limitations:
-----------------------------
- GPU performance may be very low; As of release date, NXP is investigating
  this issue as it is present on their EVK as well. Our BSP documentation explains a workaround that
  yields better performance.
- Sporadic artifacts when capturing camera images with yavta
- Video provided with the qt6demo is decoded with CPU (due to incompatible coding with VPU) and thus
  may not play smoothly.
- network boot only works with connection on ETH1 by default. Changes to the U-Boot environment are
  necessary to boot via nfs on ETH2

Changelog
---------
